.TH "PERCH-ALIAS" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-alias \- manage address aliases and catch\-all domains
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch alias [OPTIONS] COMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Aliases map additional addresses to an account. A catch\-all is stored as *@domain and accepts any local part for that domain.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Plus\-addressing (user+tag@domain) works without an explicit alias.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add
add an alias or catch\-all
.TP
.B remove
remove an alias
.TP
.B list
list aliases for an account
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch alias add \-\-account you@example.com \-\-address sales@example.com

perch alias add \-\-account you@example.com \-\-catch\-all \-\-address example.net

perch alias list \-\-account you@example.com
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1), \fBperch\-alias\-add\fR(1), \fBperch\-alias\-list\fR(1), \fBperch\-alias\-remove\fR(1)
